   "id": "thermocouple-k",
   "title": "K-Type Thermocouple",
   "subtitle": "Type K \u00b7 exposed bead junction \u00b7 yellow mini plug",
   "w": 182,
   "h": 66,
   "notes": "TC1 in hardware/BOM.csv \u2014 NOT PURCHASED (TASK-1), so the caller should render this ghosted. The yellow body is the ANSI identifier for Type K and is the only reason a person can tell it from a J or T plug at a glance, so it is coloured yellow rather than a palette body colour. The two blades are drawn deliberately unequal: on a real mini plug the wider blade is the negative pin, and that asymmetry is the polarity key \u2014 a reversed pair still fits nothing but reads backwards, which is why both pin descriptions carry the warning. Low-voltage part; no mains colours. The bead is drawn oversized relative to the lead so the junction is visible at sheet scale.",
